        "value": "endangered",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "Younger Miyako speakers are L1 Japanese speakers, and L2 Miyako learners (most people under 40 who learn are involved in traditional Okinawan culture, like the theater, with a growing number of language activists). And basically no children learn it at home from their parents, though there have been efforts to establish a language nest. [Endangerment.Certainty: 1]",
        "scale": "elcat-v2024.1"
      },
